Scan deadline tests
===================

From the kernel source directory:

  ./tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run \
    --kunitconfig=drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/tests \
    'brcmfmac-scan-timeout*'

The timeout has a 10-second minimum and a 60-second maximum. A 97-channel
foreground scan receives a 24,280 ms budget. The tests cover active and
passive requests, all-band fallback, explicit channel lists and arithmetic
saturation. P2P keeps its existing deadline. Internal PNO follow-up scans
do not arm the foreground timer.

To exercise the scan entrypoints with mocked firmware and timer services:

  python3 tools/asahi/brcmfmac-scan-timeout-tests.py

BCM4378 sleep and roam
======================

  ./tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run \
    --kunitconfig=drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/tests \
    'brcmfmac-sleep-roam*'

BCM4378 does not wait for flowring txstatus. assoc_info is retried only
after -EBADE (-52), and only while a connect or roam success is expected.
Eight queries, seven 25 ms sleeps. Other chips keep the old wait and do
not retry.
